maria: Quick flag 11111 noticed the migration guide still uses raw HTTP checks in examples. v2 uses structured errors (e.g. {code: 'RATE_LIMIT'}) so we need an appendix mapping and tolerant snippets.
kevin: Agree. We should publish a canonical mapping and small py/ts snippet showing v2-first detection with v1 fallback.
nina: I'll own the docs PR. Plan: mapping table + migration appendix + update snippets under docs/snippets/*/error-handling and add CI smoke tests. Target draft EOD Thu.
sam: Snippets to paste (edit as needed):
```python
try:
  resp = client.generate(prompt)
except Exception as e:
  payload = getattr(e, 'meta', None) or getattr(e, 'body', None) or {}
  code = payload.get('code') or getattr(e, 'status_code', None)
  if code == 'RATE_LIMIT' or code == 429:
    backoff_and_retry()
  elif code == 'INVALID_REQUEST' or code == 400:
    raise
  else:
    raise
```
```ts
try {
  await client.responses.create({ input: prompt });
} catch (err) {
  const v2 = err?.response?.data?.code;
  const v1 = err?.status || err?.response?.status;
  const code = v2 ?? v1;
  if (code === 'RATE_LIMIT' || code === 429) {
    await backoffAndRetry();
  } else if (code === 'INVALID_REQUEST' || code === 400) {
    throw err;
  } else {
    throw err;
  }
}
```
kevin: Add small mapping rows in PR: 429 -> RATE_LIMIT (retryable), 502/503 -> TRANSIENT_SERVER_ERROR (retryable w/ jitter), 400 -> INVALID_REQUEST (do not retry). Also note to emit error.code in logs/alerts.
